#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-ast.md:6
msgid "The `syn` AST"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-ast.md:8
msgid ""
"The **`syn`** crate provides a complete, robust parser that parses a raw "
"`TokenStream` into structured, AST types that can represent any element of "
"Rust code. `syn` has a wide API surface, but it should feel relatively "
"straightforward as it mirrors the structure of Rust syntax itself. Here we "
"illustrate the use of `syn` for a Derive macro:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-ast.md:20
msgid "// Parse raw tokens into a structured `DeriveInput` AST:\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-ast.md:23
msgid "// Inspect struct metadata:\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-ast.md:27
msgid "// ...\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-ast.md:31
msgid ""
"**`DeriveInput`:** The standard AST structure for a struct, enum, or union."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-ast.md:32
msgid ""
"**`parse_macro_input!`:** A specialized macro helper provided by `syn` to "
"easily parse the input token stream. It automatically handles compile-time "
"syntax errors if the input is malformed. This macro accepts the name of the "
"type into which to parse the token stream after an `as` separator, notation "
"that resembles a Rust cast."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-ast.md:40
msgid "Explore `DeriveInput`, which three main components:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-ast.md:42
msgid "`ident`: The name of the struct/enum."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-ast.md:43
msgid "`generics`: Generic parameters, lifetemes, and constraints."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/writing/deps/syn-ast.md:44
msgid ""
"`data`: An enum containing `syn::DataStruct`, `syn::DataEnum`, or "
"`syn::DataUnion`, which lets you iterate over variants and fields."
msgstr ""
